   "path": "SCENE.md",
   "role": "instructions",
   "content": "# Terminal Cursor Zoom\n\nCamera locked to the typing cursor, dollying across a terminal as one command types at high zoom.\n\nCategory: ui-blocks. Length: 3 s. WebGL: no.\n\nUse when:\n- One install command is the whole beat and it must stay legible in a vertical crop: the camera holds the cursor at frame centre.\n- A short social clip needs kinetic energy from the typing itself.\n\nAvoid when:\n- The session has several lines, logs or output: use a terminal simulator; this types exactly one command.\n- The terminal window should stay statically framed.\n\nVariables:\n- command (string): Command, default \"npm run render -- --size 1080x1920\"\n- zoom (number, 1-4): Zoom, default 2.8\n- font_size (number, 10-32): Font size, default 20\n- prompt (string): Prompt, default \"$\"\n- title (string): Title, default \"~/code/promo-video\"\n- chars_per_frame (number, 0.25-4): Chars per frame, default 1\n- chunk_size (number, 1-8): Chunk size, default 1\n- speed (number, 0.25-4): Speed, default 1\n\nSource: https://github.com/Remocn/remocn. Licence: MIT. The scene file keeps the upstream notice.\n"
  },
  {
   "path": "scene.html",
   "role": "source",
   "content": "<!doctype html>\n<!--\n  Terminal Cursor Zoom\n\n  Camera locked to the typing cursor, dollying across a terminal as one command types at high zoom.\n\n  Ported to an HTML + GSAP sub-composition by usemosio/blocks from:\n  https://github.com/Remocn/remocn/blob/126221ae00ba86eb40b65731b125ff398687d3b7/registry/remocn/terminal-cursor-zoom/index.tsx\n\n  MIT License\n\n  Copyright (c) 2026 Remocn\n\n  Permission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a copy\n  of this software and associated documentation files (the \"Software\"), to deal\n  in the Software without restriction, including without limitation the rights\n  to use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, and/or sell\n  copies of the Software, and to permit persons to whom the Software is\n  furnished to do so, subject to the following conditions:\n\n  The above copyright notice and this permission notice shall be included in all\n  copies or substantial portions of the Software.\n\n  THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED \"AS IS\", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR\n  IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,\n  FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE\n  AUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER\n  LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM,\n  OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE\n  SOFTWARE.\n-->\n<html\n  lang=\"en\"\n  data-composition-id=\"terminal-cursor-zoom\"\n  data-composition-duration=\"3\"\n  data-composition-variables='[{\"id\":\"command\",\"type\":\"string\",\"role\":\"content\",\"label\":\"Command\",\"description\":\"The single command that types out.\",\"default\":\"npm run render -- --size 1080x1920\"},{\"id\":\"zoom\",\"type\":\"number\",\"role\":\"motion\",\"label\":\"Zoom\",\"description\":\"Camera zoom on the cursor.\",\"default\":2.8,\"min\":1,\"max\":4,\"step\":0.1,\"unit\":\"x\"},{\"id\":\"font_size\",\"type\":\"number\",\"role\":\"style\",\"label\":\"Font size\",\"description\":\"Terminal font size in pixels.\",\"default\":20,\"min\":10,\"max\":32,\"step\":1,\"unit\":\"px\"},{\"id\":\"prompt\",\"type\":\"string\",\"role\":\"content\",\"label\":\"Prompt\",\"description\":\"Prompt character before the command.\",\"default\":\"$\"},{\"id\":\"title\",\"type\":\"string\",\"role\":\"content\",\"label\":\"Title\",\"description\":\"Window title.\",\"default\":\"~/code/promo-video\"},{\"id\":\"chars_per_frame\",\"type\":\"number\",\"role\":\"motion\",\"label\":\"Chars per frame\",\"description\":\"Typing speed.\",\"default\":1,\"min\":0.25,\"max\":4,\"step\":0.25},{\"id\":\"chunk_size\",\"type\":\"number\",\"role\":\"motion\",\"label\":\"Chunk size\",\"description\":\"Characters revealed per step.\",\"default\":1,\"min\":1,\"max\":8,\"step\":1},{\"id\":\"speed\",\"type\":\"number\",\"role\":\"motion\",\"label\":\"Speed\",\"description\":\"Playback speed multiplier.\",\"default\":1,\"min\":0.25,\"max\":4,\"step\":0.05,\"unit\":\"x\"}]'\n>\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n    <title>Terminal Cursor Zoom</title>\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <template>\n      <link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Geist+Mono:wght@400;500&amp;display=block\" />\n      <style>\n        #root {\n          position: absolute;\n          inset: 0;\n          overflow: hidden;\n          container-type: size;\n          pointer-events: none;\n        }\n\n        #root { background: #0b0b0e; font-family: \"Geist Mono\", ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, monospace; }\n        .tz-stage { position: absolute; inset: 0; }\n        #tz-world { transform-origin: 0 0; }\n        #tz-win { position: absolute; width: 900px; height: 480px; background: #0a0a0a; border-radius: 12px; overflow: hidden; display: flex; flex-direction: column; box-shadow: 0 30px 80px rgba(0,0,0,0.6), 0 0 0 1px rgba(255,255,255,0.06); }\n        #tz-chrome { height: 40px; flex: none; background: #1a1a1a; display: flex; align-items: center; padding: 0 16px; gap: 8px; border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.06); box-sizing: border-box; }\n        .tz-light { width: 12px; height: 12px; border-radius: 50%; opacity: 0.85; }\n        #tz-title { flex: 1; text-align: center; color: #71717a; font-size: 13px; }\n        #tz-body { flex: 1; position: relative; padding: 20px; overflow: hidden; }\n        #tz-line { position: absolute; left: 20px; right: 20px; top: 20px; display: flex; align-items: center; white-space: pre; color: #fafafa; }\n        #tz-prompt { color: #22c55e; margin-right: 8px; }\n        #tz-cur { display: inline-block; background: #fafafa; margin-left: 2px; }\n\n      </style>\n\n      <div id=\"root\" data-composition-id=\"terminal-cursor-zoom\" data-duration=\"3\" data-fps=\"30\">\n        <div id=\"tz-clip\" class=\"tz-stage clip\" data-start=\"0\" data-duration=\"3\" data-track-index=\"0\">\n<div id=\"tz-world\"><div id=\"tz-win\"><div id=\"tz-chrome\"><span class=\"tz-light\" style=\"background:#ff5f57\"></span><span class=\"tz-light\" style=\"background:#febc2e\"></span><span class=\"tz-light\" style=\"background:#28c840\"></span><div id=\"tz-title\"></div></div><div id=\"tz-body\"><div id=\"tz-line\"><span id=\"tz-prompt\"></span><span id=\"tz-text\"></span><span id=\"tz-cur\"></span></div></div></div></div>\n        </div>\n\n        <script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/gsap@3.14.2/dist/gsap.min.js\"></script>\n        <script>\n          (function () {\n            \"use strict\";\n            var root = document.getElementById(\"root\");\n            var vars =\n              window.__hyperframes && window.__hyperframes.getVariables\n                ? window.__hyperframes.getVariables()\n                : {};\n            function num(value, fallback, min, max) {\n              var n = Number(value);\n              return Number.isFinite(n) ? Math.min(max, Math.max(min, n)) : fallback;\n            }\n            function str(value, fallback) {\n              return typeof value === \"string\" && value ? value : fallback;\n            }\n            function bool(value, fallback) {\n              return typeof value === \"boolean\" ? value : value === \"true\" ? true : value === \"false\" ? false : fallback;\n            }\n            function pick(value, options, fallback) {\n              return options.indexOf(String(value)) >= 0 ? String(value) : fallback;\n            }\n            function num(value, fallback, min, max) {\n              var n = Number(value);\n              return Number.isFinite(n) ? Math.min(max, Math.max(min, n)) : fallback;\n            }\n            function str(value, fallback) {\n              return typeof value === \"string\" && value ? value : fallback;\n            }\n            function bool(value, fallback) {\n              return typeof value === \"boolean\" ? value : value === \"true\" ? true : value === \"false\" ? false : fallback;\n            }\n            function pick(value, options, fallback) {\n              return options.indexOf(String(value)) >= 0 ? String(value) : fallback;\n            }\n            // Frame-based helpers, written from their definitions.\n            var Easing = (function () {\n              function bezier(x1, y1, x2, y2) {\n                return function (x) {\n                  if (x <= 0) return 0;\n                  if (x >= 1) return 1;\n                  var lo = 0, hi = 1, t = x;\n                  for (var i = 0; i < 40; i++) {\n                    var u = 1 - t;\n                    var cx = 3 * u * u * t * x1 + 3 * u * t * t * x2 + t * t * t;\n                    if (Math.abs(cx - x) < 1e-6) break;\n                    if (cx < x) lo = t; else hi = t;\n                    t = (lo + hi) / 2;\n                  }\n                  var v = 1 - t;\n                  return 3 * v * v * t * y1 + 3 * v * t * t * y2 + t * t * t;\n                };\n              }\n              return {\n                bezier: bezier,\n                linear: function (t) { return t; },\n                quad: function (t) { return t * t; },\n                cubic: function (t) { return t * t * t; },\n                sin: function (t) { return 1 - Math.cos((t * Math.PI) / 2); },\n                poly: function (n) { return function (t) { return Math.pow(t, n); }; },\n                ease: bezier(0.42, 0, 1, 1),\n                out: function (f) { return function (t) { return 1 - f(1 - t); }; },\n                inOut: function (f) { return function (t) { return t < 0.5 ? f(t * 2) / 2 : 1 - f((1 - t) * 2) / 2; }; }\n              };\n            })();\n            function interpolate(input, inR, outR, o) {\n              o = o || {};\n              var n = inR.length;\n              var left = o.extrapolateLeft || \"extend\";\n              var right = o.extrapolateRight || \"extend\";\n              var i = 1;\n              while (i < n - 1 && input > inR[i]) i++;\n              var a = inR[i - 1], b = inR[i];\n              if (input < inR[0] && left === \"clamp\") return outR[0];\n              if (input > inR[n - 1] && right === \"clamp\") return outR[n - 1];\n              var t = b === a ? 0 : (input - a) / (b - a);\n              if (o.easing) t = o.easing(t);\n              return outR[i - 1] + (outR[i] - outR[i - 1]) * t;\n            }\n            // Damped spring from rest to 1. durationInFrames stretches time so the spring has settled by then.\n            function spring(o) {\n              var c = o.config || {};\n              var mass = c.mass != null ? c.mass : 1;\n              var k = c.stiffness != null ? c.stiffness : 100;\n              var damp = c.damping != null ? c.damping : 10;\n              function at(t) {\n                var w0 = Math.sqrt(k / mass);\n                var z = damp / (2 * Math.sqrt(k * mass));\n                if (z < 1) {\n                  var wd = w0 * Math.sqrt(1 - z * z);\n                  return 1 - Math.exp(-z * w0 * t) * (Math.cos(wd * t) + ((z * w0) / wd) * Math.sin(wd * t));\n                }\n                return 1 - Math.exp(-w0 * t) * (1 + w0 * t);\n              }\n              var t = Math.max(0, o.frame) / o.fps;\n              if (o.durationInFrames) {\n                var settle = 4, step = 1 / o.fps;\n                for (var s = settle; s > 0.05; s -= step) {\n                  if (Math.abs(1 - at(s)) > 0.001) { settle = s + step; break; }\n                  settle = s;\n                }\n                t = (Math.max(0, o.frame) / o.durationInFrames) * settle;\n                if (o.frame >= o.durationInFrames) return 1;\n              }\n              return at(t);\n            }\n            function parseColor(c) {\n              var m;\n              c = String(c).trim();\n              if ((m = /^#([0-9a-f]{3,8})$/i.exec(c))) {\n                var h = m[1];\n                if (h.length <= 4) h = h.split(\"\").map(function (x) { return x + x; }).join(\"\");\n                return [parseInt(h.slice(0, 2), 16), parseInt(h.slice(2, 4), 16), parseInt(h.slice(4, 6), 16), h.length === 8 ? parseInt(h.slice(6, 8), 16) / 255 : 1];\n              }\n              if ((m = /^rgba?\\(([^)]+)\\)/i.exec(c))) {\n                var p = m[1].split(\",\").map(Number);\n                return [p[0], p[1], p[2], p.length > 3 ? p[3] : 1];\n              }\n              return [0, 0, 0, 1];\n            }\n            function interpolateColors(t, inR, outR) {\n              var a = parseColor(outR[0]), b = parseColor(outR[1]);\n              var u = Math.min(1, Math.max(0, (t - inR[0]) / (inR[1] - inR[0])));\n              return \"rgba(\" + [0, 1, 2].map(function (i) { return Math.round(a[i] + (b[i] - a[i]) * u); }).join(\",\") + \",\" + (a[3] + (b[3] - a[3]) * u) + \")\";\n            }\n            // Seeded 0..1 value: the same seed always gives the same number.\n            function random(seed) {\n              var s = String(seed), h = 2166136261;\n              for (var i = 0; i < s.length; i++) {\n                h ^= s.charCodeAt(i);\n                h = Math.imul(h, 16777619);\n              }\n              h = Math.imul(h ^ (h >>> 13), 2246822519);\n              h = Math.imul(h ^ (h >>> 16), 3266489917);\n              return ((h ^ (h >>> 15)) >>> 0) / 4294967296;\n            }\n            // Fit a fixed-size design stage into the frame.\n            function fit(el, w, h, fill) {\n              var s = Math.min(root.clientWidth / w, root.clientHeight / h) * (fill || 1);\n              el.style.position = \"absolute\";\n              el.style.left = \"50%\";\n              el.style.top = \"50%\";\n              el.style.width = w + \"px\";\n              el.style.height = h + \"px\";\n              el.style.transform = \"translate(-50%, -50%) scale(\" + s + \")\";\n              return s;\n            }\n            // Drive draw(frame) from the timeline so seeking always draws the same picture.\n            function clockTween(tl, totalFrames, draw, rate) {\n              var clock = { frame: 0 };\n              tl.to(clock, { frame: totalFrames, duration: totalFrames / 30, ease: \"none\", onUpdate: function () { draw(clock.frame * (rate || 1)); } }, 0);\n              draw(0);\n            }\n            var SVGNS = \"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\";\n            function svgEl(tag, attrs, parent) {\n              var e = document.createElementNS(SVGNS, tag);\n              for (var k in attrs) e.setAttribute(k, attrs[k]);\n              if (parent) parent.appendChild(e);\n              return e;\n            }\n\n\n                        // Stop-motion helpers: poses are held for `step` frames.\n            var DEFAULT_STEP = 3;\n            function qf(frame, step) { step = step || DEFAULT_STEP; return Math.floor(frame / step) * step; }\n            function qstep(frame, step) { step = step || DEFAULT_STEP; return Math.floor(frame / step); }\n            function hash01(seed) { return random(seed); }\n            function hashRange(seed, lo, hi) { return lo + hash01(seed) * (hi - lo); }\n            function paperJitter(frame, seed, o) {\n              o = o || {};\n              var amp = o.amp != null ? o.amp : 1.4, rotAmp = o.rotAmp != null ? o.rotAmp : 0.35;\n              var s = qstep(frame, o.step);\n              return { x: hashRange(seed + \":x:\" + s, -amp, amp), y: hashRange(seed + \":y:\" + s, -amp, amp), rot: hashRange(seed + \":r:\" + s, -rotAmp, rotAmp) };\n            }\n            function steppedRamp(frame, from, to, o) {\n              o = o || {};\n              var f = qf(frame, o.step);\n              if (f <= from) return 0;\n              if (f >= to) return 1;\n              var ease = o.ease || function (t) { return t; };\n              return ease((f - from) / (to - from));\n            }\n\n\n            function scaledStage(el, boost) {\n              var W = root.clientWidth, H = root.clientHeight;\n              var s = Math.min(W / 1280, H / 720) * (H > W ? (boost || 1.4) : 1);\n              el.style.position = \"absolute\"; el.style.left = \"0\"; el.style.top = \"0\";\n              el.style.width = W / s + \"px\"; el.style.height = H / s + \"px\";\n              el.style.transformOrigin = \"0 0\"; el.style.transform = \"scale(\" + s + \")\";\n              return s;\n            }\n\n            var world = document.getElementById(\"tz-world\");\n            var s = scaledStage(world, 1.3);\n            var SW = root.clientWidth / s, SH = root.clientHeight / s;\n            var command = str(vars.command, \"npm run render -- --size 1080x1920\");\n            var zoom = num(vars.zoom, 2.8, 1, 4), fontSize = num(vars.font_size, 20, 10, 32);\n            var prompt = typeof vars.prompt === \"string\" ? vars.prompt : \"$\";\n            var cpf = num(vars.chars_per_frame, 1, 0.25, 4), chunk = Math.round(num(vars.chunk_size, 1, 1, 8)), speed = num(vars.speed, 1, 0.25, 4);\n            document.getElementById(\"tz-title\").textContent = str(vars.title, \"~/code/promo-video\");\n            document.getElementById(\"tz-prompt\").textContent = prompt;\n            var win = document.getElementById(\"tz-win\"), textEl = document.getElementById(\"tz-text\"), cur = document.getElementById(\"tz-cur\"), lineEl = document.getElementById(\"tz-line\");\n            win.style.left = (SW - 900) / 2 + \"px\"; win.style.top = (SH - 480) / 2 + \"px\";\n            var lineH = Math.round(fontSize * 1.6);\n            lineEl.style.fontSize = fontSize + \"px\"; lineEl.style.height = lineH + \"px\";\n            cur.style.width = fontSize * 0.55 + \"px\"; cur.style.height = fontSize + \"px\";\n            var charW = fontSize * 0.6, winL = (SW - 900) / 2, winT = (SH - 480) / 2;\n            var textX = winL + 20 + prompt.length * charW + 8, curY = winT + 40 + 20 + lineH / 2;\n            var lineStart = Math.round(10 / speed);\n            function draw(frame) {\n              var local = (frame - lineStart) * speed;\n              var lin = Math.floor(interpolate(local, [0, command.length / cpf], [0, command.length], { extrapolateLeft: \"clamp\", extrapolateRight: \"clamp\" }));\n              var rev = Math.min(command.length, Math.ceil(lin / chunk) * chunk);\n              var tx = SW / 2 - zoom * (textX + rev * charW), ty = SH / 2 - zoom * curY;\n              world.style.transform = \"scale(\" + s + \") translate(\" + tx + \"px,\" + ty + \"px) scale(\" + zoom + \")\";\n              var started = frame >= lineStart;\n              textEl.textContent = command.substring(0, rev);\n              var blink = Math.floor((Math.max(0, local) / 30) * 2) % 2 === 0;\n              cur.style.display = started && rev < command.length && blink ? \"inline-block\" : \"none\";\n              lineEl.style.visibility = started ? \"visible\" : \"hidden\";\n            }\n            var tl = gsap.timeline({ paused: true });\n            clockTween(tl, 90, draw);\n\n            var total = parseFloat(root.dataset.duration || \"3\");\n            if (tl.duration() < total) tl.to({}, { duration: total - tl.duration() });\n            tl.seek(0);\n            window.__timelines = window.__timelines || {};\n            window.__timelines[\"terminal-cursor-zoom\"] = tl;\n          })();\n        </script>\n      </div>\n    </template>\n  </body>\n</html>\n"
  }
